IMPORT prelude

-- Singapore University of Social Sciences Act 2017 (Singapore) -- which company the Act is about (s 2), what the university company
-- may award (s 3), which of its acts need the Minister's prior written consent and what happens to an act done without it (s 7(1),
-- (3)), how Parliament's money may be spent (s 8(2)), the Minister's power to demand information from ANY person and the offence of
-- refusing or obstructing (s 9(2), (5)), student bodies and the Societies Act 1966 (s 10), and the Act prevailing over the company's
-- own documents (s 11(1)).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/SUSSA2017.txt. The deposit says it "incorporates all
-- amendments up to and including 1 December 2021 and comes into operation on 31 December 2021"; the only amendment it annotates is
-- [40/2018] at s 7(2). Its Legislative History names that as the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018 (amendments made
-- by section 512, commencement 30 July 2020).
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0216 in subjects/sg/requirements.jsonl: tier 3 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. The requirement asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked a
-- sharper question yet. The Act has eleven sections and mostly governs the university company itself; what reaches an outsider (a
-- student, a graduate, a counterparty, anyone holding records) is s 2 (which company this is), s 3 (degrees), s 7(3) (an act or
-- agreement made without the Minister's consent is unenforceable), s 9 (the information demand and the $1,000 offence) and s 10
-- (student bodies). SCOPED to those, with s 8(2) and s 11(1).
-- Not encoded: the accountability framework, quality assurance and external review panel (s 4), the Minister's policy directions
-- (s 5), the appointment and removal of trustees (s 6) beyond its interaction with s 7(1)(e), the duty to fund (s 8(1)), access to
-- records and the public summary of financial statements (s 9(1), (3), (4)), and s 11(2) (other written law still applies).
--
-- The ARRANGEMENT OF SECTIONS at the top of the deposit is one line out of step with the body (it lists "1." with no heading and
-- numbers "Short title" as 2); the section numbers here follow the body. The deposit's Comparative Table says s 12 of Act 30 of 2017
-- was "Omitted as having had effect" in the 2020 Revised Edition; its content is not in the deposit and is not encoded.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. NOT for public use. See NOTES.md.

§ `Singapore University of Social Sciences Act 2017`

§§ `2 -- which company is the university company`

-- s 2: "'university company' means the company limited by guarantee incorporated under the Companies Act 1967 on 14 April 2005 under
-- the name 'SIM University', which is renamed 'Singapore University of Social Sciences' on 17 March 2017."
-- The definition fixes ONE company by its incorporation, not by its current name. A different company that merely uses the name
-- "Singapore University of Social Sciences" is not the university company.
GIVEN `limited by guarantee` IS A BOOLEAN, `incorporated under the Companies Act 1967` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `incorporated on 14 April 2005` IS A BOOLEAN, `incorporated under the name SIM University` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the company is the university company` IF
        `limited by guarantee`
    AND `incorporated under the Companies Act 1967`
    AND `incorporated on 14 April 2005`
    AND `incorporated under the name SIM University`

§§ `3 -- what the university company may award`

-- s 3: "The function of the university company is to pursue, within the limits of the financial resources available to it, the
-- objects provided by its constituent documents and, in particular, to confer and award degrees, diplomas and certificates, including
-- honorary degrees and other distinctions."
DECLARE Award IS ONE OF
    `a degree`
    `a diploma`
    `a certificate`
    `an honorary degree`
    `another distinction`
    `a licence to practise a profession`

-- A licence to practise is not among the awards s 3 names; it is included as a contrast. Whether the constituent documents' objects
-- could reach it was not read (they are not deposited).
GIVEN `the award` IS A Award
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 3 names the award` IF
    CONSIDER `the award`
    WHEN `a licence to practise a profession` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `7 -- the Minister's prior written consent`

-- s 7(1): "The prior written consent of the Minister is required for -- (a) the admission of any person as a member of the university
-- company and the removal of any such member; (b) the disposal of the whole or substantially the whole of the university company's
-- undertaking or property; (c) the voluntary winding up of the university company; (d) the addition, deletion or alteration of any
-- provision of the constituent documents of the university company; and (e) the removal of any trustee from the Board."
-- (2): these "apply in addition to the requirements prescribed by the Companies Act 1967 and the Insolvency, Restructuring and
-- Dissolution Act 2018".
-- (3): "Any act done or agreement made in contravention of subsection (1) has no effect and is unenforceable at law."
DECLARE Matter IS ONE OF
    `admitting a member`
    `removing a member`
    `disposing of the whole undertaking or property`
    `disposing of substantially the whole undertaking or property`
    `disposing of part of the property`
    `a voluntary winding up`
    `a compulsory winding up`
    `altering the constituent documents`
    `removing a trustee`
    `appointing a trustee`
    `an ordinary contract for services`

GIVEN `the matter` IS A Matter
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Minister's prior written consent is required` IF
    CONSIDER `the matter`
    WHEN `admitting a member` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `removing a member` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `disposing of the whole undertaking or property` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `disposing of substantially the whole undertaking or property` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a voluntary winding up` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `altering the constituent documents` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `removing a trustee` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 7(1)(c) names only the VOLUNTARY winding up; a winding up ordered by the court is not on the list.
-- Consent must be BOTH prior and written. Consent given afterwards, or orally, does not satisfy s 7(1); the text gives no way to
-- ratify. Encoded only as what s 7(3) says. Compliance with the Companies Act 1967 and IRDA 2018 (s 7(2)) is not modelled; meeting
-- s 7 does not by itself make the act effective under them.
GIVEN `the matter` IS A Matter, `consent was given` IS A BOOLEAN, `consent came before the act` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `consent was in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 7(3) makes the act of no effect and unenforceable` IF
        `the Minister's prior written consent is required` `the matter`
    AND (NOT (`consent was given` AND `consent came before the act` AND `consent was in writing`))

§§ `8(2) -- spending Parliament's money`

-- s 8(2): "All moneys paid to the university company under subsection (1) may only be applied or expended by the university company
-- for such objects provided by its constituent documents as the Minister allows." Moneys from other sources (fees, donations) are not
-- restricted by s 8(2).
GIVEN `the money was paid under s 8(1)` IS A BOOLEAN, `the object is in the constituent documents` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the Minister allows the object` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 8(2) permits the spending` IF
        (NOT `the money was paid under s 8(1)`)
    OR  (`the object is in the constituent documents` AND `the Minister allows the object`)

§§ `9(2), (5) -- information demands and the offence`

-- s 9(2): the Minister or an authorised person "may require any person to provide any information in that person's possession, or to
-- which that person has access, that the Minister or authorised person considers necessary for ascertaining -- (a) whether moneys paid
-- to the university company under section 8 were applied or expended in accordance with that section; or (b) any other matters that
-- the Minister or authorised person requires."
DECLARE Purpose IS ONE OF
    `checking the s 8 moneys`
    `another matter the Minister requires`

-- Limb (b) is open-ended, so every purpose the Minister names qualifies. Encoded as such.
GIVEN `the purpose` IS A Purpose
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 9(2) covers the purpose` IF
    CONSIDER `the purpose`
    WHEN `checking the s 8 moneys` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `another matter the Minister requires` THEN TRUE

-- s 9(5): "Any person who, without reasonable excuse, fails to comply with any requirement of the Minister or an authorised person
-- under subsection (2), or who otherwise hinders, obstructs or delays the Minister or an authorised person in the performance of his
-- or her duties or in the exercise of his or her powers under this section, shall be guilty of an offence and shall be liable on
-- conviction to a fine not exceeding $1,000."
--
-- READING: "without reasonable excuse" sits inside the first limb, so it is encoded as qualifying the failure to comply and not the
-- hindering, obstructing or delaying. A court might read it across both limbs; the text does not settle it.
GIVEN `a requirement was made of the person under s 9(2)` IS A BOOLEAN, `the person complied` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the person had a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN, `the person hindered, obstructed or delayed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an offence under s 9(5)` IF
        (`a requirement was made of the person under s 9(2)` AND (NOT `the person complied`) AND (NOT `the person had a reasonable excuse`))
    OR  `the person hindered, obstructed or delayed`

-- The penalty is a fine only: no term of imprisonment is provided.
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 9(5) maximum fine` IS 1000

GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 9(5) provides imprisonment` IS FALSE

GIVEN `the fine` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the fine is within s 9(5)` IF
    `the fine` AT LEAST 0 AND `the fine` AT MOST `s 9(5) maximum fine`

§§ `10 -- student bodies and the Societies Act 1966`

-- s 10(1): "To avoid doubt, the Societies Act 1966 applies to any student body constituted under the provisions of the constituent
-- documents of the university company."
-- (2): "The Minister charged with the responsibility for societies may, by order in the Gazette, exempt any student body mentioned in
-- subsection (1) from all or any of the provisions of the Societies Act 1966, subject to any conditions specified in the order."
--
-- "To avoid doubt" makes s 10(1) declaratory: it confirms rather than extends. A student club NOT constituted under the constituent
-- documents is outside s 10 and is left to the Societies Act itself, which this row does not encode (so the rule below says only
-- whether s 10 applies the provision, not whether the Societies Act applies of its own force).
-- READING: an exemption with unmet conditions is treated as not displacing the provision.
GIVEN `constituted under the constituent documents` IS A BOOLEAN, `exempted from the provision by Gazette order` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the order's conditions are met` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 10 applies the Societies Act provision to the student body` IF
        `constituted under the constituent documents`
    AND (NOT (`exempted from the provision by Gazette order` AND `the order's conditions are met`))

§§ `11(1) -- the Act prevails over the company's documents`

-- s 11(1): "Any provision of the constituent documents, or any regulation of the university company made under any provision of the
-- constituent documents, that is inconsistent with any provision of this Act is, to the extent of the inconsistency, void."
-- s 2: "'constituent documents' ... means the memorandum of association and articles of association of the university company".
DECLARE Instrument IS ONE OF
    `a provision of the memorandum or articles`
    `a regulation made under the constituent documents`
    `a contract with a third party`

-- A contract is not an instrument s 11(1) reaches; a contract made in breach of s 7(1) is dealt with by s 7(3) instead.
GIVEN `the instrument` IS A Instrument, `it is inconsistent with the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 11(1) makes it void to the extent of the inconsistency` IF
        `it is inconsistent with the Act`
    AND CONSIDER `the instrument`
        WHEN `a contract with a third party` THEN FALSE
        OTHERWISE TRUE
